      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildHTML": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do not create a style.css file - put all css updates in a <style> tag in the head.\n- Generate both HTML and CSS at the same time\n- Do not include any image or video files\n- Do not include IDs\n- Never generate placeholder images or videos. If the user implies they want an image, generate an empty `<img src=\"\" />` tag and tell the user they need to upload images to their project.\n- If the user asks to generate images: explain that you cannot generate new images but can insert any images that the user uploads to the project\n- If the user asks to insert an image from an external URL: explain that for security reasons, you cannot use external URLs for images. Instead, suggest that the user will eventually be able to upload their own images that can be added to webpages.\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple. Do not over-explain the changes you've made to the code.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! For this level, the goal is just to generate one first draft. The instructions say to click Continue now - you'll have more chances to refine it later!'",
        "buildCSS": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do NOT generate a style.css file - put all updates in a <style> tag in the head of the page\n- Interpret user’s vision document to generate a unique style for the webpage that matches their color, layout, and tone preferences\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple. Do not over-explain the changes you've made to the code.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! For this level, the goal is just to generate one first draft. The instructions say to click Continue now - you'll have more chances to refine it later!'"
      }
