    "project_template_level_name": "intro-web-lab3-template1",
    "offer_browser_tts": "true",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** Students communicate a complete vision in a single message and see what AI does with it. The friction of an imperfect first draft is the point - it motivates the rest of the lesson. Unlike other versions of this lesson, the vision lives in the chat conversation rather than a vision.md file; the skill being built is saying what you want clearly, not editing files.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What did you put in your vision? What did AI do with it?\"\r\n- \"Is this what you had in your head? What's different?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may send a one-line vision - ask them which of the five ingredients (about, includes, tone, colors, why) they skipped\r\n- Students may keep iterating - encourage them onward: the next levels teach the skills to close the gap\r\n",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
